// Negative (#49): `field` is a RESERVED keyword — the dyn-field constructor
// `field(p)` — not an identifier. Using it as a variable name (natural in a CSV
// parser; the Wanderer customer's exact case) must be a CLEAN, BOUNDED
// diagnostic, NOT a hang. The parser used to enter the `field(` argument loop
// with no `(` and spin forever (that loop advanced only when it stored an arg).
// This fixture pins the diagnostic AND, via the diag harness timeout, the
// never-hangs property. See @internal-note: known-issues #49.
fn main() -> i32 {
    var field: i32 = 0;
    field = field + 1;
    return field;
}
